            <ArticleTitle>Management of disseminated bladder tumors.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>237-47</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In summary, the management of the patient with disseminated bladder tumors can tax the knowledge and skills of the urologist who must also orchestrate and utilize the expertise of others in an attempt to prolong useful survival with chemotherapy while striving to provide maximum comfort by the prompt palliation of a variety of symptoms and problems which can occur.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
